1
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,800
My name is Arjun.

2
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,800
I have a desire to become an actor...

3
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,200
A dream.

4
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,200
But I couldn't get that opportunity anywhere.

5
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:50,000
I thought I should create my own opportunity.

6
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,500
That's why I'm writing this story.

7
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,000
A story for me.

8
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,500
My own story.

9
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,500
The title of this story...

10
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
I had gone to attend an audition for the role of a stammerer in a pilot film.

11
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:31,000
Didn't you call me for the audition saying it was a mute character, sir?

12
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:36,000
Now what's this about a stammerer?

13
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:44,500
What's the connection between acting mute and stammering, sir?

14
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:50,000
Why do you people sideline people like us, sir?

15
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:58,500
I too have a desire to act, sir.

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,500
But I just can't get an opportunity anywhere.

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,800
Even Mr. Bean stammers, sir.

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,500
He too was turned away from place to place, just like this.

19
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:29,200
But he succeeded today because of his self-confidence.

20
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:35,500
Hrithik Roshan... he stammers too, sir.

21
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:40,500
But look how big a star he is today, sir!

22
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:53,500
I... I can do it too, sir.

23
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:03,000
But I just can't get an opportunity anywhere...

24
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,500
But there's one thing, sir...

25
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:30,500
No matter what anyone says, I... I won't stop.

26
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:39,000
But someday, I will surely win.

27
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,000
Can I leave now, sir?

28
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,500
But that day, at that place, the opportunity for my talent was rejected.

29
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,800
That opportunity went to someone with no talent at all.

30
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,500
The reason behind all this is money.

31
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,500
That day, I understood one thing.

32
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:03,000
Today, if we want a fair opportunity, talent alone isn't enough... we need money too.

33
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:07,000
Hey brother, what happened at the audition?

34
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:11,500
You have no right to say any of this.

35
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:17,800
Who plays the hero, who plays the villain, where the audition is held, how it's run — that's my decision.

36
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:21,500
I'm the one putting up the money; he's the one making the film.

37
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,000
Who are you to interfere in this? Get out!

38
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:30,000
Why are you glaring? It's my story. I know who should play the hero.

39
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:35,000
He gave two lakh rupees. You give three lakh, and I'll make you the hero.

40
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,800
What kind of deal is this?

41
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,200
Hey... stop it! Ugh... this is nothing but a racket!

42
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:44,500
Have you no shame? Is this how you run an audition?

43
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Do you even know what an audition means?

44
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:52,500
Gathering a hundred or two hundred people and giving the opportunity to whoever has real talent — that's what an audition is.

45
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,800
What you're doing is just business!

46
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,500
You've turned cinema, an art form, into a business.

47
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,500
By taking money after money, you've shut out anyone who actually has talent!

48
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,500
Then why even hold something called an audition?

49
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:11,500
Wouldn't it be simpler to just put up a banner saying, "Bring the cash, take the opportunity"?

50
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,800
Why even call it an "audition"?

51
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,000
It would still be somewhat bearable if...

52
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:22,300
...it weren't for every person who leaves their hometown with no money to eat, no place to sleep, sleeping on station platforms,

53
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:27,500
still carrying the ache of "someday I'll be a hero, someday I'll see my own face on screen."

54
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:32,000
If their lives are being ruined, it's people like you who are the reason!

55
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,800
Please, learn to give opportunities to those who actually have talent!

56
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:41,000
This is exactly why I told you before — don't get into this, it's not meant for us.

57
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:45,500
You said "don't get into this, it's not meant for us" so easily, brother.

58
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:50,500
Only the one carrying that dream knows what that pain feels like.

59
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,500
All of you only see the struggle up until someone succeeds.

60
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:58,000
But I only see the joy that comes after I win.

61
00:05:58,200 --> 00:06:01,000
Until then, none of the hardship I go through is visible to you.

62
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,500
Today, when I went for the audition, I built a character.

63
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,500
He has a stammer.

64
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:11,000
But even knowing how much trouble he has, that character says he will surely win one day.

65
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,500
It's that very stammerer I look to as my life's inspiration.

66
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,200
Even if it's not today,

67
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:22,000
someday, I will surely hear the words "Action... Cut" with my own ears.

68
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:25,500
It will happen soon... I will make it happen.

69
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
If the opportunity for our talent gets rejected,

70
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:36,200
we must create our own opportunity. That's what it means to be wise.

71
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:40,200
That's why I decided I must create my own opportunity.

72
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,500
I'm creating it... and I will keep creating it.

73
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:49,500
We must never give up our effort or our talent for anyone's sake.

74
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:55,500
Many may mock our effort,

75
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:58,500
call it a foolish thing.

76
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:03,500
But only we know just how powerful our dream truly is.

77
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:07,000
Standing aside and mocking is easy,

78
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,000
making the effort is far harder.

79
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:13,500
The reward for that effort will surely arrive one day.

80
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:19,800
"Even if fate does not favor you, effort itself will always pay its wages."
